{"id": "EUVD-2026-103893", "enisaUuid": "e0e7c5bc-497b-3d61-82e0-e271aa274876", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: systemport: Fix buffer overflow in bcm_sysport_get_stats()\n\nWhen running on SYSTEMPORT Lite, certain statistics are unsupported and\nskipped during bcm_sysport_get_stats(). The variable 'j' tracks the\ncompacted index into the destination data buffer, whereas 'i' iterates\nover all elements in bcm_sysport_gstrings_stats.\n\nBecause the buffer allocated by ethtool is sized only according to\nbcm_sysport_get_sset_count(), storing values at data[i] instead of\ndata[j] writes past the allocated array bounds, leading to memory\ncorruption.\n\nFix this by writing to data[j] instead of data[i].", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:48:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:57:08", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/96a2b042051553df0d9f03b518dd3b7105b36935", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/29d1d35ad5ad379a904263ea1cd4ba1d71cd965f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/96d8b26be5bc451188acdcee055948da45adbde0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/faba9fdde480356f4a1d3b1a5713b7b354858a1c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eb7b84af0ec5c71b4920e999611b466b3784496c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98808", "GHSA-887q-3qpv-x22r"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02112003-04ef-30eb-9dfd-3840e0e987fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "049ee293-5268-3cda-b837-e7c1dd978aa1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "10377ba7673d19e28d92846955d51f49acd25c35 <96d8b26be5bc451188acdcee055948da45adbde0"}, {"id": "2708e6b3-3b15-3693-ad02-ff5e3bdf387c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "28505ba7-28ff-32ac-8613-ee79a402c6f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "45dca758-ec7f-3413-b5a9-781c75299632", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "10377ba7673d19e28d92846955d51f49acd25c35 <faba9fdde480356f4a1d3b1a5713b7b354858a1c"}, {"id": "473db0b3-4c7f-3d5b-a4c3-78cd7ab0fbde", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.14"}, {"id": "54d8910d-a572-31e2-b6f9-e3e48d7c3328", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "8481f122-6257-384f-b81e-d57dc37a5a0c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "10377ba7673d19e28d92846955d51f49acd25c35 <29d1d35ad5ad379a904263ea1cd4ba1d71cd965f"}, {"id": "b7a880f9-2bc0-3ed4-ba6f-e340663347d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "10377ba7673d19e28d92846955d51f49acd25c35 <eb7b84af0ec5c71b4920e999611b466b3784496c"}, {"id": "d33c0fd2-c08d-3407-b227-be186d18974f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "dd431b1e-1f27-3053-ab77-1376850195a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "df2068e1-c125-37f0-a73f-a3258985a75d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "10377ba7673d19e28d92846955d51f49acd25c35 <96a2b042051553df0d9f03b518dd3b7105b36935"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d7f1cb60-e0cd-3f98-989d-f553fd612554", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}